// Layer_Data_Storage — Data Storage Layer (layer 3 of 9)
// Manual render: https://app.eraser.io > Diagram-as-code (cloud architecture).
//   Create a NEW canvas named "Layer_Data_Storage".
// Export the PNG to materials/reports/figures/Layer_Data_Storage.png
// Reference: subsec:lapisan-storage (Section IV.3, sec:arsitektur-terintegrasi); tool
//   detail for the layer in row 3 of tab:layanan_industri. Included as fig:layer-storage.
// Focus: Lakehouse {MinIO (+KES), lakeFS, Apache Iceberg, Lakekeeper} and
//   Databases {ClickHouse, PostgreSQL (CNPG), MySQL, OpenSearch}; the feature service is now
//   its own layer (Layer_Feature_Service).
// Icons: product logos from docs.eraser.io/docs/icons (checked 2026-07-11):
//   minio, clickhouse, postgres, mysql, opensearch; the rest are generic icons.
//   All storage edges are oriented along the data write direction.
// Rendering MUST be horizontal (direction right), two subgroups SIDE BY SIDE, at most
//   two rows of nodes per group, without \rotatebox in LaTeX.
// Layer basis: the group label carries its source category (najafabadi2024analysis),
//   namely storage and versioning.
// Implementation check: storage/ (minio + security/kes, lakefs, lakekeeper,
//   clickhouse, cnpg + postgresql, mysql), data-governance/opensearch. Iceberg =
//   the table format realized by the Lakekeeper catalog on top of MinIO.

direction right

// Output producer (boundary)
Data Ingestion and Processing Layer [icon: download, color: orange, label: "Data Ingestion and Processing Layer (Spark, dbt)"]

// Data Storage Layer
Data Storage Layer [icon: database, color: green, label: "Data Storage Layer (storage and versioning)"] {
  Lakehouse [icon: layers] {
    MinIO [icon: minio, label: "MinIO (object + KES)"]
    lakeFS [icon: git-branch, label: "lakeFS (data versioning)"]
    Iceberg [icon: layers, label: "Apache Iceberg (table format)"]
    Lakekeeper [icon: book, label: "Lakekeeper (REST catalog)"]
  }
  Databases [icon: database] {
    ClickHouse [icon: clickhouse, label: "ClickHouse (OLAP)"]
    PostgreSQL [icon: postgres, label: "PostgreSQL (CNPG)"]
    MySQL [icon: mysql, label: "MySQL"]
    OpenSearch [icon: opensearch, label: "OpenSearch (logs + text search)"]
  }
}

// Consumers (boundary)
Feature Service Layer [icon: package, color: green, label: "Feature Service Layer"]
Model Lifecycle Layer [icon: refresh-cw, color: purple, label: "Model Lifecycle Layer"]
Data Governance Layer [icon: book, color: teal, label: "Data Governance Layer"]

// Lakehouse storage flow (data write direction)
Iceberg > MinIO: table files on object storage
lakeFS > MinIO: versioned objects
Lakekeeper > Iceberg: table metadata catalog

// Processing output lands
Data Ingestion and Processing Layer > Iceberg: write batch table
Data Ingestion and Processing Layer > ClickHouse: gold model and aggregation

// Storage consumers (data read and write direction)
ClickHouse > Feature Service Layer: offline source
Model Lifecycle Layer > PostgreSQL: MLflow metadata
Model Lifecycle Layer > MySQL: Kubeflow Pipelines and Katib metadata
Data Governance Layer > OpenSearch: write search index
